#!/bin/sh
# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Mariotaku <git@mariotaku.me> and the Beanjar contributors
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
# Headless (no graphics yet): stands in for LG's Live TV binary (com.webos.app.livetv and the
# other TV-input apps), bootd's first app in Normal mode, which sam launches as a native app. The
# stock binary sets QT_QPA_PLATFORM=wayland itself (qputenv, first thing in main) and qFatal()s in
# QWaylandDisplay, as no compositor serves /tmp/xdg/wayland-0 here: WT1H aborted with a crash
# report every boot, the later firmwares exited 1. sam's launch, and with it bootd's
# firstAppLaunched, stay as they are; the app then ends cleanly.
#
# Before it ends it sends bootd's banner-ready, as the stock app does: its first channel or input
# banner calls com.webos.bootManager/generateSignal {"name":"banner-ready"} 0.5 s after it shows
# (qml/TvComponent/Banner/{ChannelBanner,InputBanner}, Model/AppStatus.qml; the same QML in all
# six firmwares). In Normal mode bootd waits 15 s for it after its launch of this app has
# succeeded, and that wait gives init-boot-done, which holds WebAppMgr, pulseaudio, webos-jail and
# the connman adapter. On webOS 3 and 4 bootd sends minimal-boot-done only after init-boot-done, so
# a stand-in on minimal-boot-done always came after the 15 s; bootd keeps a signal that comes
# before its wait (its event table: "event is already completed"), so sending at launch is safe.
luna-send -n 1 luna://com.webos.bootManager/generateSignal '{"name":"banner-ready"}' </dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1
exit 0
